ederal government's digital platform for public services and inter-entity data exchange, designed to facilitate interoperability while operating under LGPD compliance. Its role as an integration platform puts it at the nexus of data flows across public sector entities, making LGPD compliance essential for all cross-domain data sharing facilitated by GOV.BR. This alignment reduces fragmentation and supports standardized privacy controls across agencies. This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: Relationships (429); Data: Entities (436, 46); Data: Entities (581)];\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"summary\": \"Privacy governance is strengthened by ISO 27701 integration\",\n        \"explanation\": \"ISO 27701 extends privacy information management to complement LGPD, creating a structured privacy-management framework that aligns privacy controls with the data-protection requirements of LGPD. The relationship between LGPD and ISO 27701 is established in the community as a governance mechanism that helps organizations implement, monitor, and improve privacy practices in a scalable way. This integration is further supported by the broader security context (ISO 27001) and its privacy-privacy-management extension. This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: Relationships (471); Data: Entities (481); Data: Entities (480); Data: Relationships (472)].\"\n      }\n    ,\n      {\n        \"summary\": \"Public health research data is governed under controlled LGPD conditions\",\n        \"explanation\": \"PESQUISA EM SAÚDE PÚBLICA appears as a domain where public-health research can access personal data under controlled conditions, with anonymization or pseudonymization applied where feasible. This reflects LGPD’s intent to balance research needs with privacy protections, ensuring essential studies can proceed without exposing identities. The arrangement demonstrates how LGPD’s bases and safeguards operate in sensitive c